{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03N7", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$n \\in \\mathbf{N} = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, \\ldots\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nH_\\etale^2 (\\mathbf{P}^1_\\mathbf{C}, \\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z}) =\n\\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z}.\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X(\\mathbf{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\dim_{\\mathbf{F}_q} H_\\etale^{2i} (X, \\mathbf{F}_q) =\n\\dim_{\\mathbf{F}_q} H_{Betti}^{2i} (X(\\mathbf{C}), \\mathbf{F}_q).\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nH_\\etale^2 (\\mathbf{P}^1_\\mathbf{C}, \\mathbf{Z}) = 0.\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$H_{Betti}^2(\\mathbf{P}^1(\\mathbf{C}), \\mathbf{Z}) = \\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathbf{P}^1(\\mathbf{C})$", "MATH_0009": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:575d27dbac55416705df3dabb0c6220ddb284e143944bd606c379b097256fa07", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b6167377d9f24302d2519123105e5a69a61d950be947f3c9f5b7d0f128c01af", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor a natural number <MATH_0001> it is true that\n<MATH_0002>\nMore generally, if <MATH_0003> is a complex variety, then its <ACCENT_0001>tale Betti numbers\nwith coefficients in a finite field agree with the usual Betti numbers of\n<MATH_0004>, i.e.,\n<MATH_0005>\nThis is extremely satisfactory. However, these equalities only hold for torsion\ncoefficients, not in general. For integer coefficients, one has\n<MATH_0006>\nBy contrast <MATH_0007>\nas the topological space <MATH_0008> is homeomorphic to\na <MATH_0009>-sphere.\nThere are ways to get back to nontorsion coefficients from torsion ones by a\nlimit procedure which we will come to shortly.\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6daa6c091eeb15fb42d3ed19781843613d4fa9e45a9827286a8460477969ad40", "unit_id": "tag:03N7:prose-0001"}
